From: LinBox <linbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] LinBox box64: static-binary exit fix backport (v0.3.2..v0.4.3)

Upstream v0.4.4 hasElfInterp backport: for STATIC binaries (no PT_INTERP)
RDX must be 0, not the exit bridge, at process entry - else glibc's
__libc_start_main registers the bridge with __cxa_atexit and the emulation
dies mid-exit (buffered stdout never flushed, exit code = truncated bridge
address; reproduced with a vanilla pre-0.4.4 static printf binary).

Anchor (3 lines, whitespace-insensitive via -l):
    "SetRDX(emu, Pop64(emu));    // RDX is exit function" / "}" / "DynaRun(emu);"
This sequence exists ONLY in the emulate() epilogue of v0.3.2..v0.4.3:
  - v0.3.0 ends with Run(emu, 0) and has no { } block (covered by 0006);
  - v0.4.4+ interleaves "if(!box64_hasinterp) SetRDX(emu, 0);" between the
    SetRDX and the "}", breaking the sequence - and upstream already carries
    the fix natively there, so skipping is exactly right.
Requires 0001 (declares linbox_hasinterp); sort order applies it first.
---
diff --git a/src/core.c b/src/core.c
--- a/src/core.c
+++ b/src/core.c
@@ -1564,4 +1564,16 @@
         SetRDX(emu, Pop64(emu));    // RDX is exit function
     }
+    // LinBox backport of upstream v0.4.4 fix: for STATIC binaries (no
+    // PT_INTERP) RDX must be 0, not the exit bridge. The SysV process-entry
+    // ABI passes rtld_fini in RDX; glibc's __libc_start_main registers it
+    // with __cxa_atexit, and __run_exit_handlers calls atexit handlers
+    // BEFORE RUN_HOOK(__libc_atexit) (_IO_cleanup, the stdio flush). With
+    // the exit bridge in RDX the emulation ended inside the rtld_fini call:
+    // buffered stdout was never flushed (empty output) and the exit code
+    // became the truncated bridge address (128). Upstream v0.4.4 gates this
+    // on box64_hasinterp right after the Push64/SetRDX pair above; this
+    // backport applies the same SetRDX(emu,0) right before DynaRun starts
+    // the program.
+    if(!linbox_hasinterp) SetRDX(emu, 0);
     DynaRun(emu);
     // Get EAX
